From: linux-toolchain maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] support portable linkers and backport glibc BZ #16381

Teach the pinned crosstool-NG backend about the exact Mold release selected by
linux-toolchain.  The source archive remains downloaded and verified by the
producer before the network-disabled build starts.  Link the Mold executable
fully statically so it does not retain the builder's glibc as a runtime
dependency.

The static-binutils path builds Gold directly after configure-host.  Build the
two generated prerequisites that a direct Gold build cannot make through its
own subdirectory Makefile.

Backport upstream glibc commit 798212a01311491d5e14fcda687460b75f8ca286
(BZ #16381) to the 2.17 and 2.19 package series. Explicit ld.so execution then
loads a PIE main program as an executable and runs its constructors exactly
once.

